From: =?utf-8?b?Ik1hcmNvIFRyZXZpc2FuIChUcmV2acOxbyki?= <mail@3v1n0.net>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 17:24:54 +0200
Subject: authPrompt: Reset the verifying state when an authentication step
 completed

In authPrompt we've the concept of verification state, now we set the
state to "in progress" as soon as some step is started, however we never
reset the value back to verifying once we got a reply.

This, with the current mechanisms switch support implies that it's not
possible to switch mechanism while one is in progress, and this is
particularly problematic when a MFA setup is used, where multiple steps
are acting with multiple UI requests; and an user should be free to
switch mechanism even if just a factor has been processed.

This is fine while a mechanism is checking the backend for a result, but
once we got a result we should go back to the verifying state, so that
changing mechanisms is always possible even if an authentication started.

In fact our UI allowed this, but this was currently blocked.

So introduce a new signal that auth services can emit in order to notify
that the current step has been completed and so the state can go back
to the verifying.

We cannot manage this from auth prompt itself since since answering a
query does not imply that the step is done, as PAM or any other
underlying service may take a while to answer, and we want to keep the
state in progress during that phase
